Subject: [PATCH 12/12] dt-bindings: arm: cpus: describe qcom,freq-domain and qcom,lmh-dcvs

The Khaje device trees (Xiaomi topaz/tapas, port Android 6.12) set two
Qualcomm vendor properties on each cpu@N node: qcom,freq-domain, which points
to the cpufreq-hw provider with #freq-domain-cells, and qcom,lmh-dcvs, which
points to the LMh DCVS node of the CPU's cluster. Neither property is
documented in arm/cpus.yaml of the 6.12 base, so dt-schema reports them as
unknown properties with an undecoded phandle type.

Describe both properties so that dtbs_check accepts the curated Khaje CPU
nodes. This is a minimal binding; it does not change the cpufreq-qcom-hw or
qcom-lmh drivers.

Draft without Signed-off-by; not for upstream submission.

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/arm/cpus.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/arm/cpus.yaml
index f308ff6..682a946 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/arm/cpus.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/arm/cpus.yaml
@@ -367,6 +367,21 @@ properties:
       formed by encoding the target CPU id into the low bits of the
       physical start address it should jump to.
 
+  qcom,freq-domain:
+    $ref: /schemas/types.yaml#/definitions/phandle-array
+    description:
+      Phandle and frequency domain specifier of the Qualcomm CPUFREQ hardware
+      provider that scales this CPU, as described in
+      cpufreq/cpufreq-qcom-hw.yaml (#freq-domain-cells). Consumed by the
+      Khaje device trees; one entry per CPU cluster domain.
+
+  qcom,lmh-dcvs:
+    $ref: /schemas/types.yaml#/definitions/phandle
+    description:
+      Phandle to the Limits Management Hardware (LMh) DCVS node that manages
+      the cluster containing this CPU. The phandle points to the first CPU of
+      the LMh cluster; see thermal/qcom-lmh.yaml.
+
 if:
   # If the enable-method property contains one of those values
   properties:
